commit 672421ed5a6aaf35e94ea74e6cf8ad5495f024df

C03: a recall can follow its own save in one case, and «me gusta tomar» saves the favourite drink it recalls (MEMORY1599)

«Como me llamo» and «que me gusta tomar» need a prior save in the same profile, and every case profile is born empty with the private memory disabled. The conductor host gains `turn.memory-then` {cmd,text,caseId,expectedOperation,followup}: the scripted explicit save runs first through the private-memory activation handshake (the save fails memory_disabled, the channel asks to enable, «confirmar» enables and saves; its request and completion are emitted as the two «request» phases), then the scripted recall runs as an ordinary turn whose terminal is the case's final; nothing follows a save that did not complete. `NaturalMemoryRequestParser` learns the favourite-drink save («recuerda que me gusta tomar mate», «… mi bebida favorita es el mate», «remember I like to drink …») under the `favorite_drink` selector that «que me gusta tomar» already recalled — until now that phrase was stored as a generic fact the recall could not find — and the recall forms «qué me gusta tomar», «cuál es mi bebida favorita», «what's my favorite drink».

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


